From c6320eae6caeccd65bbdb4563b4a8ee756d3fc76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:37:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] SEO: prerender guide bodies and collections; guides
 link to listings

- Guides are rendered from their own React components at build time, so the
  prerendered HTML carries the full comparison tables and write-ups (5-7.7K
  characters, up from about 850) plus the same Article/FAQPage JSON-LD the app
  sets.
- Guide comparison tables link each programme to its HSO listing where one
  exists, with the programme name as the anchor (11 links, checked by a test).
  Guide dateModified moves to 2026-10-28.
- The collections index and all 19 curated collection pages are prerendered
  with their programme lists, get shared metadata (title, description,
  ItemList + BreadcrumbList JSON-LD) used by both the app and the HTML, and
  are now in sitemap-collections.xml.
- seo-check accepts an <h1> with attributes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015eydvdzcxBPZCXsPy7MGLS
